WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.471
Typing long column names exactly right can be hard.

2
00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:10.998
In this lesson, you will learn attach, which lets RStudio suggest column names as you type.

3
00:00:10.998 --> 00:00:16.708
You will also learn what the masking messages mean, so they never worry you.

4
00:00:16.708 --> 00:00:18.340
Let's make typing easier.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.480
Here is our script so far.

6
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.520
I add a new note: attaching a dataset.

7
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.420
It eases selecting column names.

8
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.548
The function is attach.

9
00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:36.320
Attach Dataset, and then attach Demographic.

10
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.476
Run them.

11
00:00:45.476 --> 00:00:47.803
The console shows some red text:

12
00:00:47.803 --> 00:00:50.518
the following objects are masked. Don't worry.

13
00:00:50.518 --> 00:00:55.948
It means both tables have columns with the same names, so R tells us

14
00:00:55.948 --> 00:00:57.500
which one comes first.

15
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.321
Now let's see why attach helps.

16
00:01:07.321 --> 00:01:09.942
I write a new select line:

17
00:01:09.942 --> 00:01:13.000
Demographic underscore one, arrow, Dataset, pipe, select.

18
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.220
Inside select, I start typing: provin.

19
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.900
RStudio shows a list:

20
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.580
Province Name, from Dataset.

21
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.620
I just press Enter, and the full name is written for me.

22
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.164
No spelling mistakes, no missing spaces.

23
00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:16.680
This saves a lot of time with long survey column names.

24
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.320
I add Sex of household head, and Marital Status of household head, the same way.

25
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.491
Run it, and Demographic one appears in the Environment:

26
00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:06.440
three hundred fifty two rows, three columns.

27
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.171
One tip:

28
00:03:08.171 --> 00:03:11.941
attach is helpful while you explore, but it can cause confusion if you attach many tables.

29
00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:13.355
When you are done, use detach.

30
00:03:13.355 --> 00:03:15.711
That brings us to the end of our R sessions.

31
00:03:15.711 --> 00:03:16.889
You have learned so much.

32
00:03:16.889 --> 00:03:18.067
Thank you, and keep practicing!

